Melting glaciers and calving icebergs force adults to abandon historic sites. Observations from NASA Earth Observatory show some colonies temporarily shifting onto nearby icebergs or ice shelves, though these new locations often expose birds to harsher winds and fewer food sources. 
Back to the mating grounds, the time has passed, and it is time for the eggs to hatch. It's been months since the male penguins started incubating eggs, and it’s almost time for them to hatch. The egg under Gino’s care has hatched, and he hasn't eaten in this entire time and won't be able to until his partner returns.<br>
