Gino, like other male penguins, has been feeding his chick crop milk, which is a curd-like secretion triggered by the hormonal chemical prolactin. With the females now returning, the colony is more packed, with the females trying to locate their partner and chicks. Gino’s partner has found him, and Gino is more than eager to go back to the sea to hunt. But before that, the female must take care of the chick, having it perch on her feet, shielding it from the cold.<br>
